1
00:04:51,111 --> 00:04:57,111
Forbidden to remember. Terrified to forget.

2
00:09:42,222 --> 00:09:48,222
The Twilight Saga: New Moon is a adventure, fantasy,
drama film directed by Chris Weitz.

3
00:14:33,333 --> 00:14:39,333
Forks, Washington resident Bella Swan is reeling from the departure of her vampire love,
Edward Cullen, and finds comfort in her friendship with Jacob Black, a werewolf.

4
00:19:24,444 --> 00:19:30,444
But before she knows it, she's thrust into a centuries-old conflict, and her desire to
be with Edward at any cost leads her to take greater and greater risks.

5
00:24:15,555 --> 00:24:21,555
Bella Swan, played by Kristen Stewart.

6
00:29:06,666 --> 00:29:12,666
Edward Cullen, played by Robert Pattinson.

7
00:33:57,777 --> 00:34:03,777
Jacob Black, played by Taylor Lautner.

8
00:38:48,888 --> 00:38:54,888
Jane, played by Dakota Fanning.

9
00:43:40,000 --> 00:43:46,000
Aro, played by Michael Sheen.

10
00:48:31,111 --> 00:48:37,111
Alice Cullen, played by Ashley Greene.

11
00:53:22,222 --> 00:53:28,222
The Twilight Saga: New Moon is a 2009 American vampire romantic fantasy film directed by Chris Weitz from
a screenplay by Melissa Rosenberg, based on the 2006 novel New Moon by Stephenie Meyer.

12
00:58:13,333 --> 00:58:19,333
It is the sequel to Twilight (2008) and the second
installment in The Twilight Saga film series.

13
01:03:04,444 --> 01:03:10,444
The film stars Kristen Stewart, Robert Pattinson, and Taylor Lautner, reprising their
roles as Bella Swan, Edward Cullen, and Jacob Black, respectively.

14
01:07:55,555 --> 01:08:01,555
In the film, Bella gets closer with Jacob, who is a werewolf, after Edward leaves her, but when the
vampire decides to take a drastic move, she must make a decision between the two.

15
01:12:46,666 --> 01:12:52,666
Summit Entertainment announced it had greenlit the film on November
22, 2008, following the early success of Twilight.

16
01:17:37,777 --> 01:17:43,777
Principal photography began on March 23, 2009, in Vancouver,
Canada, and ended in Montepulciano, Italy on May 29.

17
01:22:28,888 --> 01:22:34,888
The Twilight Saga: New Moon premiered at the Mann Village Theater in Westwood, California on November 16,
2009, and was theatrically released in the United States on November 20, by Summit Entertainment.

18
01:27:20,000 --> 01:27:26,000
The film received generally negative reviews from critics, but grossed $711
million worldwide, becoming the seventh-highest-grossing film of 2009.

19
01:32:11,111 --> 01:32:17,111
It set domestic box office records as the biggest midnight opening in the United States and Canada,
grossing $26.3 million, which was superseded by its sequel, The Twilight Saga: Eclipse.

20
01:37:02,222 --> 01:37:08,222
This led to the highest single-day domestic gross on an opening day, with $72.7 million,
until it was beaten by Harry Potter and the Deathly Hallows – Part 2 (2011).

21
01:41:53,333 --> 01:41:59,333
The film also became the widest independent release, playing in 4,024
theaters, until it was surpassed by The Twilight Saga: Eclipse.

22
01:46:44,444 --> 01:46:50,444
New Moon was released on DVD and Blu-ray on March 20, 2010.

23
01:51:35,555 --> 01:51:41,555
As of July 2012, the film has grossed $184.9 million in North American DVD sales, selling more than 8.8 million units, four
million of which were sold within its first weekend, beating Twilight's 3.8 million units sold in its first two days.

24
01:56:26,666 --> 01:56:32,666
The film was followed by three more sequels, The Twilight Saga: Eclipse, The Twilight Saga: Breaking Dawn –
Part 1, and The Twilight Saga: Breaking Dawn – Part 2, in 2010, 2011, and 2012, respectively.

25
02:01:17,777 --> 02:01:23,777
The film explores themes of moon, based on novel or
book, vampire, teen movie, werewolf.

26
02:06:08,888 --> 02:06:14,888
The tone is emotional.
